WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.852
CROP makes three main contributions.

00:00:03.932 --> 00:00:07.783
First,

00:00:07.863 --> 00:00:11.715
it defines two certification criteria for
reinforcement learning: robustness of the per-state action,

00:00:11.795 --> 00:00:15.647
and a lower bound on the cumulative reward.

00:00:15.727 --> 00:00:19.578
Second, it turns each criterion into an algorithm.

00:00:19.658 --> 00:00:23.510
CROP-LoAct uses local randomized smoothing to
certify a radius around each state within

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.442
which the chosen action cannot change.

00:00:27.522 --> 00:00:31.373
CROP-GRe uses global smoothing to bound the
expected and percentile reward,

00:00:31.453 --> 00:00:35.305
and CROP-LoRe performs an adaptive tree search to
produce a much tighter absolute lower bound on reward.

00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:39.237
Third,

00:00:39.317 --> 00:00:43.168
the authors apply these tools to nine existing
robust RL algorithms across four environments,

00:00:43.248 --> 00:00:47.100
and release the results as an open leaderboard for
the community.
